Cell["Export eeeeAA to C++", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"10180362-6982-55dd-ae31-2544d11a5a3c"],

Cell["\<\
The helicity expressions above are combined in one C++ process. Equivalent \
placements of the identical photons are filled automatically.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc7c5ff8-a99b-5b3b-884e-3428b2fbdf5e"],

Cell["\<\
eeeeAAExport = WriteSPINASProcess[
  FileNameJoin[{spinasOutputDirectory, \"eeeeAA\"}],
  {\"e\", \"E\"} -> {\"e\", \"E\", \"A\", \"A\"},
  {
    {{\"e\", \"E\", \"E\", \"e\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"}, qed6FourFermionsPP},
    {{\"e\", \"E\", \"E\", \"e\", \"A.+\", \"A.-\"}, qed6FourFermionsPM},
    {{\"e\", \"E\", \"E\", \"e\", \"A.-\", \"A.-\"}, qed6FourFermionsMM}
  }, factorizationModel,
  \"ProcessName\" -> \"eeeeAA\",
  \"Build\" -> True, \"RunExamples\" -> True,
  \"Overwrite\"->True,
  \"CalcHEPDirectory\" -> calcHEPDirectory,
  \"CalcHEPModel\" -> calcHEPModel,
  \"CalcHEPAllowedParticles\" -> referenceParticlePDGs,
  \"MadGraphDirectory\" -> madGraphDirectory,
  \"MadGraphModel\" -> madGraphModel,
  \"MadGraphAllowedParticles\" -> referenceParticlePDGs,
  \"CalcHEPPoints\" -> validationPoints,
  \"MadGraphPoints\" -> validationPoints,
  \"RunCalcHEPValidation\" -> True,
  \"RunMadGraphValidation\" -> True,
  \"ReturnDetails\" -> True];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028063500322523`*^9, 4.0028063552951527`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"52cb1a12-3ac0-502b-a60f-960d370629cf"],

Cell["Factoring repeated scalar factors preserves the signed two-line currents. With seed 861811, CalcHEP agreed at all 1,000 spin-summed points and MadGraph agreed at 1,000 points for each of the four photon-helicity assignments.", "Text"],

Cell["Reference run for the compact two-line currents, seed 6182401. CalcHEP agreed at all 1,000 spin-summed points. MadGraph agreed at 1,000 points for each of the four photon-helicity assignments. The largest relative differences were 3.69 x 10^-13 for equal helicities and 3.71 x 10^-13 for opposite helicities.", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
The independent tests use the constructive expressions above. Full export and \
validation diagnostics remain in eeeeAAExport; a reference formula is never \
substituted. If an export already exists, add \"Overwrite\" -> True \
deliberately to refresh it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1af0ae66-e77d-56b9-b249-7d2085765df8"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

